Subject: [PATCH 04777/11362] [outer-loop] Generation-energy on ARC: structural
 conclusion (energy is selection, ARC wall is generation)

Operator chose "generation energy on ARC (the wall)". Rigorous verify-before-build (workflow
arc-borrowable-techniques-not-done-before + direct artifact reads) found the axis structurally closed to
energy models: (1) efficiency-energy comprehensively nulled (proto_carnot_pruner wash; value-routing
exp4652/4665 no live lift; state-energy AUROC 0.4958 = chance; frame-change CNN +0.184 already banked);
(2) generation-energy is the most-swept axis, all nulled by WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE; (3) the one
"genuinely-new" angle (firing info-gain active-probe; exp4727 was a non-test, posterior never built) is on
inspection a SELECTION mechanism DOWNSTREAM of generation -- exp4727's failure taxonomy
(mechanic_outside_hypothesis_class/probe_outcomes_aliased/budget) IS the generation wall. Energy models are
verifiers/selectors; ARC's wall is generation of the non-observable winning prefix; an energy at chance on
observable state (0.4958) cannot select or guide-generate toward a non-observable target. Productive home
for new energy = selection-bottlenecked off-ARC domains where SC isn't saturated (exp4940, arXiv:2605.18871).

